 "caption": "On launch day in 2013, the US government's Healthcare.gov let only six people sign up. Testing documents later showed the site could handle about 1,100 users at once, just before launch.\n\nCustomers don't wait for a slow site. They leave. Test with a real crowd before you go live and keep the first version simple.\n\nIf a hundred customers hit your website at once, what would happen? DM us the word CROWD and we'll check it for you.\n\n#moodbod #websitedesign #smallbusinessnamibia #windhoek #namibia\n\nSources: NBC News, ABC News and NPR (2013) on the six sign-ups; TechCrunch and the US House Oversight Committee (Nov 2013) on the 1,100-user test."
